<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan reverts to six-day working week.</title>
<headline>Pakistan reverts to six-day working week.</headline>
<dateline>ISLAMABAD 1996-11-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's caretaker government reverted to a six-day working week on Monday after more than two years of a five-day week introduced by ousted prime minister Benazir Bhutto.</p>
<p>The cabinet of caretaker Prime Minister Meraj Khalid decided to reduce the Friday-Saturday Islamic weekend to just Friday to increase the output of government departments, Information and Broadcasting Minister Irshad Ahmed Haqqani told reporters after a cabinet meeting.</p>
<p>Bhutto had introduced the five-day week in June 1994 but increased daily working time, saying it would save money for the government in terms of electricity and petrol.</p>
</text>
